Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] fix(layout): render text beside floating header/footer pictures

A header/footer paragraph with a floating picture took the picture branch. When
it had no treat-as-char controls, that branch laid out the picture and then laid
out the paragraph only for a page AutoNumber. Ordinary text stayed in the import
model but produced no TextLine/TextRun, so it was absent from both screen and
PDF rendering. Lay out the same composed paragraph whenever ordinary text is
present too, preserving the existing picture and AutoNumber paths.

IeumOffice patch onto v0.8.7 (not proposed upstream yet).
---
 src/renderer/layout.rs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/renderer/layout.rs b/src/renderer/layout.rs
index 5a4a3f7d2..9b31c7e18 100644
--- a/src/renderer/layout.rs
+++ b/src/renderer/layout.rs
@@ -5133,4 +5133,6 @@ impl LayoutEngine {
-                    if has_page_auto_number {
+                    // Ordinary text can share the paragraph too; it must go through
+                    // the same composed-paragraph path as the page AutoNumber (#7333).
+                    if has_page_auto_number || !para.text.is_empty() {
                         let text_end = self.layout_paragraph(
                             tree,
                             area_node,
